\n 3405: #    obvious per-call schemas; the tool fills scaffolding. â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€\r\n 3406: class _CreatePlanIn(BaseModel):\r\n 3407:     recipe_id: str\r\n 3408:     step_id: str\r\n 3409:     shape: str\r\n 3410:     goal: str\r\n 3411:     # v7 WS3 (Â§2.4b/Â§2.5b) â€” MEASURED governance, stamped at authoring.\r\n 3412:     # review_policy: {triggers: [named risk triggers], justify: {action_id:\r\n 3413:     #   one-line reason}} â€” once stamped, every leg_kind=\"review\" action must\r\n 3414:     #   have a justify entry (the anti-blanket-review gate in add_action).\r\n 3415:     # test_budget: {unit: <scope>, integration: [seams], e2e_max: N} â€” the\r\n 3416:     #   stamped pyramid; test_lineage_report counts layers against it.\r\n 3417:     # Both optional: omitting keeps full legacy behavior.\r\n 3418:     review_policy: dict | None = None\r\n 3419:     test_budget: dict | None = None\r\n 3420:     # F25 (2026-08-17, s4 wedge): REOPEN a TERMINAL plan for its reopened\r\n 3421:     # step. A step edited for new work (o5 continuity fix) while its plan sat\r\n 3422:     # terminal-succeeded had NO legal author surface â€” the plan_id is\r\n 3423:     # deterministic (<recipe>-<step>), so a fresh plan cannot be minted and\r\n 3424:     # a terminal plan refused re-create. reopen=true resets the terminal\r\n 3425:     # plan to DISPATCHING, clears terminal_status, bumps attempt, PRESERVES\r\n 3426:     # every done action (history stays honest), and worklogs the reopen â€”\r\n 3427:     # the planner then add_action's the new work (a8â€¦).\r\n 3428:     reopen: bool = False\r\n 3429: \r\n 3430: \r\n 3431: class CreatePlan(_ClaudeTool):\r\n 3432:     \"\"\"Create an empty drafted plan for a recipe step. plan_id and\r\n 3433:     domain are filled by the tool (domain inherited from the recipe);\r\n 3434:     you supply only shape + goal. Then call add_action per action â€” no\r\n 3435:     monolithic plan object, no schema guess