{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$f='\"'claude/src/edp_claude/mcp_server.py';\"'$c=Get-Content $f;for($i=80;$i -lt 185;$i++){'\"'{0,4}: {1}' -f (\"'$i+1),$c[$i]}; $f='\"'claude/src/edp_claude/store/attribution.py';\"'$c=Get-Content $f;for($i=0;$i -lt $c.Count;$i++){'\"'{0,4}: {1}' -f (\"'$i+1),$c[$i]}'","aggregated_output":"  81: \r\n  82: def build_mcp(root: Path | None = None):\r\n  83:     \"\"\"Build a FastMCP server registering every tool in the registry.\r\n  84: \r\n  85:     `mcp` is imported lazily so importing this module (e.g. for the unit\r\n  86:     test that asserts the registry wiring) does not require the SDK.\r\n  87:     \"\"\"\r\n  88:     from mcp.server.fastmcp import FastMCP\r\n  89: \r\n  90:     root = root or _agent_home()\r\n  91:     ctx = _build_context(root)\r\n  92:     tools = build_registry(ctx)\r\n  93: \r\n  94:     # DESIGN-v6 W4 (per-role tool registration): scope the registered surface\r\n  95:     # to EDP_ROLE, GOVERNED BY EDP_ROLE_SCOPE (warn|enforce, DEFAULT enforce â€”\r\n  96:     # DESIGN-v7 P0, user ruling 2026-07-12: the derived floors were audited\r\n  97:     # all through v6, the last known enforce-break (the reviewer-leg\r\n  98:     # role=\"worker\" default, d67/d100) is closed by P4.1, so warn-mode is now\r\n  99:     # the opt-OUT, not the milestone). F37#5 (2026-08-18) â€” identity fails\r\n 100:     # CLOSED: `toolset_for_role` returns None only for an ABSENT role, and\r\n 101:     # the full registry registers only for a NON-SPAWNED shell (no\r\n 102:     # EDP_HANDLE â€” the operator console / tests). A SPAWNED shell with a\r\n 103:     # missing role, or ANY shell with an unknown EDP_ROLE value, refuses to\r\n 104:     # build: both are spawn-env bugs that used to silently grant the full\r\n 105:     # surface.\r\n 106:     #\r\n 107:     #   warn (opt-out, EDP_ROLE_SCOPE=warn): ALL tools register â€” NO\r\n 108:     #     filtering. A call to a tool OUTSIDE the role's scoped set is\r\n 109:     #     recorded as a role_scope_violation worklog event (role + tool name)\r\n 110:     #     and then PROCEEDS. The observe-before-enforce Phase-1 bar, kept as\r\n 111:     #     the diagnostic mode.\r\n 112:     #   enforce (default, v7): the registry is FILTERED to exactly the\r\n 113:     #     role's ROLE_TOOLSETS (an off-set tool is simply absent).\r\n 114:     #\r\n 115:     # Drift between a role toolset name and the LIVE built registry\r\n 116:     # (ALL_TOOL_CLASSES) fails CLOSED in BOTH modes, with NO name special-cased:\r\n 117:     # we refuse to build a mis-scoped server rather than silently drop a tool a\r\n 118:     # role expects, or pass a name that no longer resolves (a hardcoded\r\n 119:     # carve-out would be the exact fail-open o7 forbids).\r\n 120:     role = (os.environ.get(\"EDP_ROLE\") or \"\").strip() or None\r\n 121:     allowed = toolset_for_role(role)\r\n 122:     if role is not None and allowed is None:\r\n 123:         # F37#5: an UNKNOWN role value (typo, stale spawner) must never\r\n 124:         # silently register the full surface.\r\n 125:         raise RuntimeError(\r\n 126:             f\"edp-claude: EDP_ROLE={role!r} is not a known role \"\r\n 127:             \"(tools/roles.py ROLE_TOOLSETS) â€” refusing to build a \"\r\n 128:             \"full-surface server for an unrecognised identity. Fix the \"\r\n 129:             \"spawn env, or unset EDP_ROLE for an operator console.\")\r\n 130:     if role is None and is_spawned():\r\n 131:         raise RuntimeError(\r\n 132:             \"edp-claude: this shell carries EDP_HANDLE (pool-spawned) but \"\r\n 133:             \"no EDP_ROLE â€” a spawned shell without its role would \"\r\n 134:             \"otherwise inherit the operator's full tool surface (F37#5). \"\r\n 135:             \"Fix the spawn env; only a non-spawned operator console may \"\r\n 136:             \"run role-less.\")\r\n 137:     scope_mode = (os.environ.get(\"EDP_ROLE_SCOPE\", \"enforce\").strip()\r\n 138:                   or \"enforce\")\r\n 139:     if scope_mode not in (\"warn\", \"enforce\"):\r\n 140:         # F37#12: EDP_ROLE_SCOPE is a strict enum. Every unknown value used\r\n 141:         # to fall through to warn behaviour â€” a typo ('enfroce') silently\r\n 142:         # registered the full surface in observe-only mode.\r\n 143:         raise RuntimeError(\r\n 144:             f\"edp-claude: EDP_ROLE_SCOPE={scope_mode!r} is not a known \"\r\n 145:             \"mode â€” use 'enforce' (default) or 'warn'. Refusing to guess: \"\r\n 146:             \"an unknown value must never silently open the surface.\")\r\n 147:     off_scope_names: set[str] = set()\r\n 148:     if allowed is not None:\r\n 149:         registered = {t.name for t in tools}\r\n 150:         missing = allowed - registered\r\n 151:         if missing:\r\n 152:             raise RuntimeError(\r\n 153:                 \"edp-claude role-toolset drift for \"\r\n 154:                 f\"EDP_ROLE={role!r}: tools/roles.py \"\r\n 155:                 f\"names {sorted(missing)} that are not registered tools in \"\r\n 156:                 \"ALL_TOOL_CLASSES. Reconcile roles.py with the built \"\r\n 157:                 \"registry â€” refusing to build a mis-scoped server rather \"\r\n 158:                 \"than silently drop tools a role expects.\"\r\n 159:             )\r\n 160:         if scope_mode == \"enforce\":\r\n 161:             # F1 (owner ruling 2026-08-17): off-role tools are ABSENT â€” no\r\n 162:             # refusal stubs. The Phase-3c stubs kept every off-scope tool\r\n 163:             # visible in the listing (\"(not available to role=â€¦)\"), which\r\n 164:             # re-bloated the system prompt with ~60 schemas and tempted\r\n 165:             # shells toward verbs they could never use. A mis-scoped call\r\n 166:             # now surfaces as the harness's own unknown-tool error; the\r\n 167:             # role's card names its surface, and the broker route\r\n 168:             # (ask_above/notify_above) remains the answer to \"I need a verb\r\n 169:             # another role owns\".\r\n 170:             tools = [t for t in tools if t.name in allowed]\r\n 171:         else:\r\n 172:             # warn: keep the full surface; the off-set tools get a shim that\r\n 173:             # logs a role_scope_violation on call, then proceeds.\r\n 174:             off_scope_names = registered - allowed\r\n 175: \r\n 176:     # Lazy import (like the rest of this seam): the worklog-writing helper\r\n 177:     # lives with the tools it also guards. Used only by warn-mode off-set shims.\r\n 178:     from .tools._tools import record_role_scope_violation\r\n 179: \r\n 180:     mcp = FastMCP(\"edp-claude\")\r\n 181: \r\n 182:     def _make_shim(bound_tool):\r\n 183:         # 2026-05-20 (Â§5.5 post-HITL sweep B): expose the tool's REAL\r\n 184:         # InputModel schema with FLAT top-level args â€” no `payload`\r\n 185:         # wrapper. The old shim took a single `payload: dict`, so every\r\n   1: \"\"\"Actor attribution resolved IN CODE â€” the single source of truth for\r\n   2: *who* performed a state-mutating store write (W15, DESIGN-v6).\r\n   3: \r\n   4: principle-6 (no LLM in a tool): the attribution is READ from the process\r\n   5: environment the pool stamps onto every spawned shell (`EDP_ROLE` /\r\n   6: `EDP_HANDLE`) â€” it is never supplied by a caller / model, so it cannot be\r\n   7: spoofed by a payload. This module is the ONE place that resolution lives:\r\n   8: spec_store stamps it today, and the recipe/plan stores reuse `actor()`\r\n   9: verbatim (a4) so attribution is identical across every store.\r\n  10: \"\"\"\r\n  11: \r\n  12: import os\r\n  13: \r\n  14: # The env vars the pool stamps onto a spawned shell (see /worker Step 1).\r\n  15: _ROLE_ENV = \"EDP_ROLE\"\r\n  16: _HANDLE_ENV = \"EDP_HANDLE\"\r\n  17: _UNKNOWN = \"unknown\"\r\n  18: \r\n  19: \r\n  20: def is_spawned() -> bool:\r\n  21:     \"\"\"True when this shell was stamped by the pool (`EDP_HANDLE` present).\r\n  22: \r\n  23:     F37#5 (2026-08-18): the trust pivot for role-less shells. The pool stamps\r\n  24:     BOTH vars on every spawn, so a shell with a handle but no role is a\r\n  25:     spawn-env bug (or a cleared var), never the operator console â€” role\r\n  26:     guards must treat it as UNTRUSTED, not exempt. The operator's foreground\r\n  27:     base shell has neither var and stays fully trusted.\r\n  28:     \"\"\"\r\n  29:     return bool(os.environ.get(_HANDLE_ENV, \"\").strip())\r\n  30: \r\n  31: \r\n  32: def trusted_as(role: str) -> bool:\r\n  33:     \"\"\"True when the calling shell may act as `role` for a role-gated write.\r\n  34: \r\n  35:     - `EDP_ROLE` set: exact match only.\r\n  36:     - `EDP_ROLE` absent: trusted ONLY for a non-spawned shell (the operator\r\n  37:       console / tests). A spawned shell missing its role fails CLOSED\r\n  38:       (F37#5 â€” the old ``if role and role != x`` guards skipped when the\r\n  39:       role was empty, so clearing the var was privilege escalation).\r\n  40:     \"\"\"\r\n  41:     got = os.environ.get(_ROLE_ENV, \"\").strip()\r\n  42:     if got:\r\n  43:         return got == role\r\n  44:     return not is_spawned()\r\n  45: \r\n  46: \r\n  47: def actor() -> dict:\r\n  48:     \"\"\"Resolve the acting shell's attribution from the environment.\r\n  49: \r\n  50:     Returns ``{\"role\", \"handle\"}`` â€” both non-empty (``\"unknown\"`` when the\r\n  51:     env var is unset/blank, e.g. the neuron shell has no `EDP_HANDLE`), so a\r\n  52:     worklog record always carries a concrete `by`. No LLM value ever reaches\r\n  53:     here (principle-6): the caller passes nothing.\r\n  54:     \"\"\"\r\n  55:     role = os.environ.get(_ROLE_ENV, \"\").strip() or _UNKNOWN\r\n  56:     handle = os.environ.get(_HANDLE_ENV, \"\").strip() or _UNKNOWN\r\n  57:     return {\"role\": role, \"handle\": handle}\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
