  543: \r\n  544: Loop hygiene (the freeze class): the broker's store IO runs off its\r\n  545: asyncio loop (to_thread on publish/inbox/query/message/SSE reads) Â· the\r\n  546: three hottest locked store writes in the MCP tools (next_action recipe+\r\n  547: plan saves, record_action_status) run via asyncio.to_thread. RESIDUAL\r\n  548: (recorded): remaining store writes stay sync on the loop â€” short critical\r\n  549: sections; full async-store migration is a follow-up if contention shows.\r\n  550: \r\n  551: Also: shadow tests updated to the F3 default-off contract (were\r\n  552: pre-existing reds â€” the pool suite had not run since F3).\r\n  553: \r\n  554: Suites: claude 1548 (+3), edp-pool 303 (+3), edp-broker 29 â€” all green\r\n  555: (Phoenix env-fail only). NOTE: pool/broker changes need the STACK RESTART\r\n  556: to take effect in the live fleet.\r\n  557: \r\n  558: ## F37 â€” Adversarial campaign Round 5 (role surfaces & trust), 2026-08-18\r\n  559: 12 findings (raw: .sol_review_out-r5.txt). Threat-model ruling (owner,\r\n  560: 2026-08-18): single-operator local fleet â€” the adversary is a confused or\r\n  561: prompt-injected AGENT, never a hostile local process. CONFIRMED 7 + the\r\n  562: cheap halves of 2; REJECTED the multi-tenant auth infrastructure.\r\n  563: \r\n  564: | # | Finding | Verdict |\r\n  565: |---|---------|---------|\r\n  566: | 5 | unset/unknown EDP_ROLE fails open to full registry | CONFIRM â€” fixed |\r\n  567: | 12 | EDP_ROLE_SCOPE typo falls to warn-mode | CONFIRM â€” fixed |\r\n  568: | 9 | worker mutates actions in a foreign plan | CONFIRM â€” fixed |\r\n  569: | 11 | planner CRUD checks type, not ownership | CONFIRM â€” fixed |\r\n  570: | 10 | worker composes broker_send via observe(effect=) | CONFIRM â€” fixed |\r\n  571: | 1 | role-less shell can mint acceptance_verdict | PARTIAL â€” spawned-role-less refused; operator console kept |\r\n  572: | 6 | agent-authored text framed as instructions | CONFIRM â€” envelopes shipped |\r\n  573: | 4 | broker unauthenticated | provenance-metadata half TAKEN; auth half REJECTED (single-operator) |\r\n  574: | 8 | secrets inherited into every shell | env-hygiene half TAKEN (strip + redact); isolated bridge service DEFERRED until a keyed HTTP delegate exists |\r\n  575: | 2 | pool control-plane unauthenticated | REJECT â€” out of scope for a single-operator localhost fleet (revisit if ever exposed) |\r\n  576: | 3+7 | headless --dangerously-skip-permissions / acceptor write reach | OWNER RULING: keep acceptor EDIT (fix-what-it-safely-can); headless-skip is what headless means here |\r\n  577: \r\n  578: Identity fails CLOSED: attribution.is_spawned()/trusted_as() are the one\r\n  579: trust pivot (EDP_HANDLE = pool-stamped); build_mcp REFUSES an unknown\r\n  580: EDP_ROLE and a spawned shell with no role; EDP_ROLE_SCOPE is a strict\r\n  581: enum (unknown aborts; in-tool guard treats non-'warn' as enforce) Â· the\r\n  582: neuron-only guards (north_star_update, global facts) and the acceptor\r\n  583: verdict guard use trusted_as, so an absent role on a spawned shell is\r\n  584: untrusted, not exempt. Ownership: record_action_status refuses a worker\r\n  585: writing outside its handle's plan (grounding echo now unskippable);\r\n  586: update/delete_object bind a planner to its OWN plan's objects. Effects:\r\n  587: observe/register_rule refuse an effect action outside the initiating\r\n  588: role's toolset (driver re-checks at arm). Framing (#6): specialist\r\n  589: groundings carry a provenance banner (single-doc bit-for-bit superseded);\r\n  590: recipe briefs open with a rendered-data framing line; check_inbox returns\r\n  591: a `framing` field on every delivery; shadow briefs framed as dispatcher\r\n  592: claims; worker card gains the framing law; acceptor card marks its brief\r\n  593: sender-authored. Provenance (#4 half): HttpBroker.send stamps\r\n  594: body._sender {role, handle} from the server env at the one outbound seam